## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical skills in implementing observability across Kafka-based event streaming pipelines—a critical real-world challenge as data flows through multiple topics and partitions.

## Key Concepts
- W3C Trace Context propagation across messaging systems
- Span continuity across producer/consumer boundaries
- Sampling strategy selection and trace baggage for correlation
- Observability during partition rebalance and backpressure scenarios

## Code Example
```javascript
// Inject trace context into outgoing message headers
function injectTraceContext(payload, tracer) {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('produce_order');
  const carrier = {};
  tracer.inject(span.context(), W3C_TRACE_CONTEXT, carrier);
  return { payload, headers: carrier };
}

// Extract trace context from incoming message
function extractTraceContext(message, tracer) {
  const spanContext = tracer.extract(W3C_TRACE_CONTEXT, message.headers);
  const span = tracer.startSpan('process_order', { childOf: spanContext });
  return span;
}

// Attach trace_id to enriched payload for cross-topic correlation
function enrichWithTraceId(payload, span) {
  return { ...payload, trace_id: span.spanContext().traceId };
}
```

## Key Considerations
- Use OpenTelemetry for vendor-agnostic instrumentation
- Ensure trace context propagation survives partition rebalances
- Consider tail-based sampling for cost-effective tracing of rare errors
- Monitor latency degradation during rebalance events

## Why This Is Asked

To test understanding of consumer rebalances and offset management, a common pitfall for beginners where duplicates occur if offsets aren't tracked during rebalances.

## Key Concepts

- Consumer group rebalancing
- Per-topic offset tracking
- In-flight state
- Safe commit on revoke
- Timeouts and fault tolerance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo code showing API hooks
class RebalanceSafeConsumer {
  constructor() { this.committedOffsets = new Map(); this.inFlight = new Set(); }
  onPartitionsAssigned(parts) { for (const p of parts) { const k = `${p.topic}:${p.partition}`; const start = (this.committedOffsets.get(k) ?? -1) + 1; this.seek(p.topic, p.partition, start); } }
  onPartitionsRevoked(parts) { const revoked = new Set(parts.map(p => `${p.topic}:${p.partition}`)); /* wait for inFlight on revoked before committing */ }
  processMessage(msg) { const id = `${msg.topic}:${msg.partition}:${msg.offset}`; this.inFlight.add(id); // downstream write then:
    this.inFlight.delete(id); const key = `${msg.topic}:${msg.partition}`; this.committedOffsets.set(key, msg.offset); }
  commitOffsets() { /* commit logic here */ }
}
```

